Subject: [PATCH 12/19] Sensor-side zoom: implement setVieWindow, add set_zoom

Reads a window of the OV2640 in SVGA mode (2x the detail of the CIF mode
the 240x240 stream uses) and scales it to the output size. set_zoom
{x, y, size} in SVGA pixels over serial or POST /api/set/zoom/; size 0
restores the full view. Not saved. Gain/exposure are re-applied after each
mode switch since it rewrites the register tables.

Measured (XIAO OV2640, 240x240): full view 66.8 fps, zoomed 33.3 fps -
SVGA mode reads twice the lines per frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
